<%# @spec CHAT-API-008 @spec CHAT-API-009
    The viewport bound is applied from the controller with a measured
    `--chat-panel-offset-top` variable instead of a fixed subtraction
    so layout chrome above `<main>` (notably notice/alert flashes)
    still leaves the conversation pane as the real scroll container.
    Below `lg` the page carries no bottom padding at all (`pt-4`, no
    `pb-*`) and `--chat-panel-bottom-space` is `0`, so the panel runs
    flush to the viewport edge — every mobile pixel goes to the
    transcript. At `lg`+ the page keeps symmetric `py-8` padding and
    the panel subtracts the matching `2rem`. dvh (not vh) so the iOS
    Safari URL bar doesn't shrink the available space.

    This must be a definite `height`, never a `max-height`, and must
    carry no `min-h` floor. A `max-height` leaves the panel's own
    height `auto` — indefinite — so percentage heights below it do not
    resolve: the shared conversation partial's `h-full` root falls
    back to its natural content height, overflows the
    `min-h-0 flex-1 overflow-hidden` wrapper below, and the transcript
    is clipped mid-conversation with the input unreachable and nothing
    scrollable. A `min-height` is equally wrong here: against a height
    already fitted to the viewport it can only clamp the panel taller
    than the viewport, which is the document-scroll failure this bound
    exists to prevent.
    (@spec CHAT-API-008, CHAT-API-009, #3459, #3575, #3635) %>
<div class="flex flex-col overflow-x-hidden"
     data-controller="chat"
     data-chat-session-id-value="<%= chat_session.id %>"
     style="height: calc(100dvh - var(--chat-panel-offset-top, 0px) - var(--chat-panel-bottom-space, 2rem));">
  <%# The chat page is chat-first: the only always-visible chrome is a
      single compact line — the title and a "Session details" toggle —
      so the transcript and composer stay the dominant region of the
      viewport-bound panel. Everything else (project chips, updated
      timestamp, capability badge, runner/model selectors, token usage,
      archive/unarchive buttons) lives inside the closed `Session
      details` disclosure. The `Workspace` disclosure remains a sibling
      and keeps its existing open-by-default rule for non-inline chats
      so the recovery path stays reachable. (@spec CHAT-API-009, #3925) %>
  <header class="relative z-10 shrink-0 border-b border-gray-200 px-4 py-2 xl:hidden" data-chat-header="mobile">
    <details class="group">
      <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-2 [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
        <h1 class="min-w-0 truncate text-base font-semibold text-gray-900" title="<%= chat_session_title(chat_session) %>"><%= chat_session_title(chat_session) %></h1>
        <span class="flex shrink-0 items-center gap-1 text-xs font-semibold text-gray-600">
          <span>Session details</span>
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 text-gray-400 transition group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19 9-7 7-7-7" />
          </svg>
        </span>
      </summary>
      <%= render "session_details",
                 chat_session: chat_session,
                 dom_id_suffix: "_mobile",
                 can_update_chat_session: can_update_chat_session,
                 can_archive_chat_session: can_archive_chat_session,
                 can_unarchive_chat_session: can_unarchive_chat_session,
                 available_runners: available_runners,
                 available_models: available_models %>
    </details>

    <%= tag.details class: "group mt-1 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-gray-50",
                    open: !chat_session.inline_only? do %>
      <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500 transition hover:text-gray-800 [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
        <svg class="h-3.5 w-3.5 text-gray-400 transition group-open:rotate-90" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m9 5 7 7-7 7" />
        </svg>
        Workspace
      </summary>
      <div class="px-2 pb-2">
        <%= render "capability_panel", chat_session: chat_session, dom_id_suffix: "_mobile" %>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </header>

  <%# A workspace disclosure can be taller than the panel on a short desktop
      viewport. Keep its controls in the header's scrollable region instead
      of allowing the conversation flex item to cover them. (@spec CHAT-API-009) %>
  <header class="relative z-10 hidden max-h-[75%] shrink-0 overflow-y-auto border-b border-gray-200 px-4 sm:px-6 xl:block" data-chat-header="desktop">
    <details class="group">
      <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-2 py-2 [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
        <h1 class="min-w-0 truncate text-base font-semibold text-gray-900" title="<%= chat_session_title(chat_session) %>"><%= chat_session_title(chat_session) %></h1>
        <span class="flex shrink-0 items-center gap-1 text-xs font-semibold text-gray-600">
          <span>Session details</span>
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 text-gray-400 transition group-open:rotate-180" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19 9-7 7-7-7" />
          </svg>
        </span>
      </summary>
      <%= render "session_details",
                 chat_session: chat_session,
                 dom_id_suffix: "",
                 can_update_chat_session: can_update_chat_session,
                 can_archive_chat_session: can_archive_chat_session,
                 can_unarchive_chat_session: can_unarchive_chat_session,
                 available_runners: available_runners,
                 available_models: available_models %>
    </details>

    <%# Collapsed for inline-only chats: the capability panel's
        cloned-repo list grows without bound, and inside a
        viewport-bound panel an unbounded header starves the
        transcript. Sessions that actually have a workspace render it
        open, because the panel then holds the only controls for that
        workspace — "Reopen with workspace" is a stopped chat's sole
        recovery path, and folding it away leaves the chat looking
        unrecoverable. Open by default (not on click) so it works
        before, and without, JavaScript. (@spec CHAT-API-009) %>
    <%= tag.details class: "group mt-1 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-gray-50",
                    open: !chat_session.inline_only? do %>
      <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center gap-1.5 px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500 transition hover:text-gray-800 [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
        <svg class="h-3.5 w-3.5 text-gray-400 transition group-open:rotate-90" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m9 5 7 7-7 7" />
        </svg>
        Workspace
      </summary>
      <div class="px-2 pb-2">
        <%= render "capability_panel", chat_session: chat_session %>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </header>

  <div class="min-h-0 flex-1 overflow-hidden px-4 pb-1 pt-1 sm:px-6 sm:pt-5">
    <%= render "conversation",
               chat_session: chat_session,
               chat_messages: chat_messages,
               has_older_messages: has_older_messages %>
  </div>
</div>
